(2210383, 301731, 21714, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by xion:</b></div><hr/><i> I like this shot. I like the processing too, expect that I think that highlights have gone a bit too far on the right. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>By right I actually meant left! :) There is something about the shot that I like very much. I don''t agree that every single shot of a mother with child should be soft or display excellence in sharpness. After all it''s not about proving how good a camera or lens is.</td>', 'Originally posted by xion: I like this shot. I like the processing too, expect that I think that highlights have gone a bit too far on the right.   By right I actually meant left! :) There is something about the shot that I like very much. I don''t agree that every single shot of a mother with child should be soft or display excellence in sharpness. After all it''s not about proving how good a camera or lens is.', '2006-03-08 07:56:07.000000', NULL, 0),
